WEBVTT

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:17.040
Hozuki!

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.790
We aren't together!

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:30.160
No way... What should I do?
It's because he protected me!

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.160
I'd hate for it to end like this!

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.120
I'd absolutely hate it!

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.120
That's right.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.410
What am I doing... not believing in
the decision I made until the end?!

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.410
It's okay.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:48.660
The notes will definitely...
play where we want them to!

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:52.200
Wh-What is this?! They're playing
totally different than before!

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.000
I'm not alone anymore.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.660
Don't you dare try and "match" our level, okay?

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.830
Just play with all you've got!

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:04.700
That's it. I'll lead in my own way.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.830
Of course I will.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:10.910
Once I found it, I couldn't <i>not </i>get involved...

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:14.120
...with the sound that sways
my heart so intensely.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:32.370
What on earth... just happened?

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:39.040
"#14    A Step Forward"

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:05.040
Their performance got really good
halfway through, didn't it?

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.870
The audience is super excited.

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:12.450
I-It's okay! We can still
outdo them! Right, Mio?!

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:18.620
Mio...?

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:22.700
Mio is laughing out loud?!

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.080
I've never seen that before! How creepy!

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:29.450
Don't roll around in a place like this!
Hey, it's our turn next, you know!

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:30.660
President...

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:36.910
I can give my best performance ever today.

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:40.410
The first half and the second half...

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:43.540
It seemed as if they were played
by two different schools.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:46.750
Then they showed their real
ability in the second half?

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:52.450
Their tone was quite different from
what I expected. It was profound...

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.200
You look happy, Ousuke.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.250
What? I do?

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:00.870
Sen... Their performance was
kinda amazing, wasn't it?

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:02.080
Yeah...

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.370
Hey! Don't be so impressed, you stupid Haru!

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.870
Compared to us, they're nothing!

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:09.160
What? But--

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.330
Shut up!

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:14.830
My goodness... I feel like
I saw something very incredible.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:18.200
They did a great job
recovering in the second half.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:21.410
I feel like their performance lifted my spirits.

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:24.790
We were able to witness someone's growth.

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:27.660
We're lucky to hear a performance like this.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:32.040
Their performance was great.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:36.580
Chika did a good job... though he
worried me at the beginning.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:38.450
Would you like to use this?

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.200
Thanks, Mom.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.410
What?

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:43.750
Are you okay, Kazusa?

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.830
I'm not okay.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:50.000
I can't accept a performance like that.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.660
I'm sorry!

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.200
What?

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:02.080
Hey, what's going on?
What's up with you three?

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:05.290
Ah, well, Kudo was actually...

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.040
Since I've been having a bad case of diarrhea,

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:16.580
I couldn't focus and
dragged you down. I'm sorry.

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:20.500
I-I knew about it,
but I didn't tell you guys.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:21.500
Same here.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:24.370
Don't tell such an obvious lie.

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:25.870
M-Mr. Takinami!

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:28.330
What? A lie? What're you talking about?

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:29.830
--Ow!
--Whoa... It looks worse than earlier.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:32.830
--Whoa... It looks worse than earlier.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.120
Chika! Your hand...!

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.290
Oh, no! What happened?

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:40.290
Could it be from that time...?

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:43.160
He hurt himself in the restroom.

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:44.250
What?

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.370
Since he didn't look well,

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:49.790
I threw him into the restroom and
told him he didn't have to perform.

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:52.660
Then he snapped and hit the wall,
injuring his hand.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:57.250
It was so lame that even I can
understand why he wanted to lie.

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:58.080
You bastard...!

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:01.330
Hm? Am I mistaken?

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:05.120
Y-You're not... mistaken.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:07.620
Jeez... How lame!

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:08.700
That's our Chika!

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.160
You're so funny, Chika!

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.370
Stop playing around and
go get your hand treated.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:15.750
I know already!

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.750
Now, you guys pack up the instruments.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.830
Sorry. I got thirsty, so I'm going
to buy something to drink.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:24.830
What? Ah... Sure.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.660
Whoa... Hozuki sure can pack up fast.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.200
K-Kurata...

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.830
Is Chika's injury really...?

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:37.620
Yeah, really, I hope it gets better soon.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:41.080
When it does, let's play together again.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:44.250
Yes.

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:47.540
"First-aid Station"

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:52.080
It'll require one month to heal.
Actually, it might take longer than that.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.910
Huh?! One month?!

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:56.160
Why?! It's just a sprain, right?

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:00.250
Don't take it lightly. Because you overdid it,
it's gotten quite a bit worse.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:04.410
Don't use that hand for a while.
Once the swelling is gone, start rehab.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:06.290
Wh-What about the koto?

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:07.910
Don't play it, of course.

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:08.620
"Shock"

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:10.870
I'll heal it up in three days!

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.200
Good luck with that. Okay, you can go now.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:18.450
Let's see... The one he's always drinking is...

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:20.580
"Strawberry Au Lait"

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:24.580
Are you looking for something?

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:32.000
What? U-Um... I-I'd like to buy the tasty
strawberry snacks. All of them!

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:36.700
"Concession Stand"

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:38.790
Ah... Kud--

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.620
Hey you, wait!

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:41.790
Ugh!

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.830
What, you again?

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:46.290
What do you want?

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:50.040
I heard your performance.
What the heck was that?!

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:53.450
You were unorganized and terrible
in the first half. I couldn't stand it.

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:55.910
It seemed that you recovered
quite a bit in the second half,

00:06:55.910 --> 00:07:00.910
but a piece is a piece when you
play it from the start till the end!

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:03.700
I can't accept that kind of performance!

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:08.870
As I thought, you're not worthy
to play the koto with Satowa!

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:14.580
You're saying that again?
Today's performance was all my fault.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.700
And, I've said this many times,

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:20.040
but Hozuki plays with us because she wants to.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.410
It's not for you to decide.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:26.500
Is that all? See ya.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.160
It's you guys' fault!

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:29.370
Huh?

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:33.700
Satowa's performance today...

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:39.200
That's... That's not how
her performance should be!

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:40.080
Huh?

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:42.580
Those tones weren't hers!

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:46.330
They used to be sharper
and more honed before!

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:49.750
They sounded strong, noble, and always solid!

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:54.450
I admired her tones so much, but now,
they've been defiled by you!

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:57.660
Because she plays with
unskilled people like you guys,

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:03.000
Satowa's tones became halfhearted!
She's not as good as she was before!

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:06.290
If you stay in this puny club,
you'll only get worse.

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:13.200
Why...? Then does it mean that I
should be facing the koto like I used to?

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:16.660
Continuing to scream all by myself...?

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:20.250
Your koto... is like a weapon to me.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:24.540
They've become gentle.

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:27.750
What?

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:32.790
It's not that they became halfhearted
or that she became a bad player.

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:36.040
It's just that her tones became gentler.

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:39.450
I like her current tones a lot more than

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:43.450
her tones when I first heard them.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:02.160
I'm not asking you what you like.

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:05.410
You don't know anything about tones!

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:09.080
They've become gentle.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:16.910
I already... know that. You don't have
to tell me 'cause I already know that!

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:22.450
From childhood, Satowa's tones
were enveloped by solitude in some way.

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:24.750
They were irresistibly beautiful.

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:27.620
They were so beautiful that they
made her unapproachable.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:30.370
They were transcendent to me.

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:34.540
But I was wrong...

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:42.330
I've never heard her tones sound so gentle,
brilliant, fun, and happy before.

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:45.120
Tones like that...

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:49.000
...would never have been born
playing with me.

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:53.200
Damn. She just said whatever she wanted.

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:56.870
Whoa! You?! How long have you been here?

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:59.580
I've been here from the beginning.

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:03.580
What do <i>you </i>know about my tones?

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:09.580
What, you were listening?
Sorry, I only said what I thought.

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:17.000
Th...

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:20.410
Thank you.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:25.660
Thank you.

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.120
Chika!

00:10:36.870 --> 00:10:38.950
There you are!

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:41.450
This is for you!

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:43.450
Huh? Wha...?

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:47.950
Hey, Chika. Is your hand okay?

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:50.540
Hm? Wasn't Hozuki just here, too?

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:56.660
Ah! You went ahead and bought snacks
already?! That's not fair! Give me some!

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:57.790
No way.

00:10:57.790 --> 00:11:01.410
How stingy! Since when
did you become so petty?!

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:02.910
Shut up.

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:18.660
That concludes all the performances
by participating high schools.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:24.500
My goodness... I never expected to see
this many high-level performances.

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:26.580
I'm glad I was able to listen to them.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:32.790
After hearing them, I started questioning
if it was okay for us to give marks.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:34.790
There's nothing we can do about it.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:39.370
Since this is a competition, we have
to decide the ranking no matter what.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:46.660
Kudo...

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:47.790
Yeah.

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:49.040
"Stare..."

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:50.870
"Stare..."
Is the person behind us your friend?

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.540
"Stare..."
A total stranger.

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:54.290
Hey... What's your name?

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:55.870
Definitely no!

00:11:55.870 --> 00:11:57.540
Then give me your contact info.

00:11:57.540 --> 00:11:58.830
No!

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:01.870
Then can I come hang out
with you at your place?

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:04.160
Four-eyes! Help me!

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:05.870
What?!

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:09.540
Your tones are... interesting.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:12.620
Your tones, I can understand.

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:13.830
What?

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:17.750
I can see the accumulated
training behind them.

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:22.330
They're refined, very beautiful tones.

00:12:22.330 --> 00:12:24.790
But your tones are mysterious.

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:27.000
They're unrefined, but for some reason--

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:30.250
Hey, Mio! You wandered off again!

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:32.950
Everyone's sitting over there. Let's go.

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:36.290
No. You sit here, too, Uta.

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:38.080
Jeez...!

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:40.450
What does "unrefined" mean?

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:46.080
Well, we're now going to announce
the results of this competition.

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:49.450
Ahh... I'm so nervous.
I'm scared of hearing the results.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:52.040
Stop it, Kota. I don't wanna
catch your nervousness!

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:56.790
Hmph! How pathetic! If you're a man,
you should remain calm!

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:58.620
You sure seem manly.

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:01.120
Shut up! You picking a fight?!

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:06.080
We heard many high-level,
memorable performances,

00:13:06.080 --> 00:13:09.000
which made this competition an amazing one.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:13.450
Judging was difficult, especially
the best performance award.

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:17.160
Well, enough with the introduction.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:19.500
We'll now move onto announcing the results.

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:27.160
First, I'll announce the seven
schools out of all 33,

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:30.830
one from each prefecture, to receive
the award for outstanding performance.

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:34.080
Then, I'll announce the school that won
first place, the best performance award,

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:36.080
out of those seven.

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:40.790
The first outstanding performance award
is for Tokyo, which goes to...

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:42.790
...Meiryo High School.

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:46.160
Great.

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:48.200
Ousuke.

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:49.450
We did it!

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:52.330
Yep.

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:58.160
Next is for Ibaraki, which goes
to Eidai Fuzoku High School.

00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:00.580
All rrrrrright!

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:03.790
Whooooa! Sen!

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:06.830
Did you hear that?!
This is the level of our ability!

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:09.580
Don't be so conceited just because you
have cute girl members!

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:11.080
S-Sen!

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:15.750
Stupid idiot. What an embarrassing guy.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:21.250
--Oh, shoot... My heart is pounding
so hard that my body is swaying.
--For Tochigi, the award goes to
Ichihara Yamaoka High School.

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:23.540
I can't breathe...

00:14:23.540 --> 00:14:27.700
--Ahh... I hope we get chosen.
--For Gunma, the award goes
to Kuriyama Daiichi High School.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:29.540
Ahh... Oh boy, oh boy...

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:30.750
--For Saitama, the award goes
to Ezawa High School.

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:33.040
--It's nerve-racking, isn't it, Mio?
--For Saitama, the award goes
to Ezawa High School.

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:34.540
Not really.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:38.660
We're not gonna lose.
I don't wanna lose... not to Tokise.

00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:41.040
It'll be fine.

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:42.700
We'll win.

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:44.160
Fumi...

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:47.910
Of course we will.

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:51.450
And lastly, for Kanagawa.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:55.000
I'm more nervous than when I'm by myself.

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.250
We did everything we could do!

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:00.950
The award goes to...

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:08.500
...Kanagawa Prefectural...

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:10.950
...Hakuto High School.

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:16.120
What?

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:18.750
We did it!

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:21.540
Haku... to...

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:25.290
"Tokise High School
Kanagawa Prefectural Hakuto High School"
What about the school going after us?
They're from Kanagawa.

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:29.500
They're the ones who played right after us!

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:33.290
We did it, Mio! We won the award!

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:38.830
Do you now feel like telling me your name?

00:15:43.950 --> 00:15:45.330
We didn't get chosen...

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:48.160
Oh, you guys didn't get chosen? How lame...

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:49.870
Hey, Sen!

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:52.500
Sorry.

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:57.950
Well, it was a natural outcome.

00:15:57.950 --> 00:16:00.950
With a mistake like that,
they can't win a competition.

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:06.000
Hakuto High School... It's the school
that performed right after Tokise...

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:11.290
Well, that's understandable...
given the kind of performance they gave.

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:16.620
What...? What just happened?

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:19.750
Hakuto? Who's that?

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:23.200
How could we lose
to an unknown school like that...?

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:28.910
And, as for the best performance award,
actually, it'll be awarded to two schools.

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:32.580
Meiryo High School from Tokyo

00:16:32.580 --> 00:16:35.790
and Hakuto High School from Kanagawa.

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:41.370
I know this is unusual,
but both schools are equally excellent,

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:46.160
so we'd like to give the best
performance award to both schools.

00:16:46.160 --> 00:16:47.790
No way! The best performance award?!

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:49.500
We did it!

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:52.250
The same level as us...

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:55.370
Well then, we'll start the award ceremony now.

00:16:55.370 --> 00:16:58.250
--This can't be happening.
--Those who are receiving the award...

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:03.000
Himesaka has been in first place
all this time in Kanagawa.

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:07.330
Kazusa...

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:28.870
What's happening...?

00:17:30.290 --> 00:17:33.870
The back of my throat feels uncomfortable.

00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:36.580
Hard to breathe...

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:39.620
It feels damn hot inside my body...

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:41.500
...like it's burning.

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:47.660
Takaoka, are you gonna go talk to Chika
and the others before you leave?

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:52.500
Ah... No, I'll go home. They probably
don't want me to talk to them right now.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:55.000
I don't think they mind.

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:57.620
But well, let's go home, then.
I'll take you home.

00:17:57.620 --> 00:17:59.700
No, thank you. I'll be fine.

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:00.700
Oh, don't be so reserved.

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:02.450
No, really, I'm fine.

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:05.040
Let's go home, Haru. What're you doing?

00:18:05.040 --> 00:18:08.120
Ah, well, I was wondering where they were.

00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:09.660
You mean those guys from Tokise?

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:14.200
Y-Yeah. I thought I wanted to
make friends with them.

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:16.790
Huh?! Don't talk nonsense!

00:18:16.790 --> 00:18:19.750
We'll see them again anyway...

00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:21.540
...as long as we continue to play the koto.

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:22.870
Sen...

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:25.200
Enough about that!
We have to go home and practice!

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:27.450
We don't have the luxury to take a break!

00:18:27.450 --> 00:18:29.830
Dammit! We couldn't even
be first place in Kanto

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:32.160
when we're aiming to be
number one in nationals...

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:35.620
We'll definitely be first place next time!

00:18:35.620 --> 00:18:38.750
Do you feel a little calmer now?

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:40.160
I'm okay.

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:49.200
This will make us stronger.

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:59.200
Hey, Mio! Where're you going?!

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:04.370
Looks like things are getting
more and more interesting.

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:14.160
Guys...

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:18.250
As expected, it's not
so easy to place, is it?

00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:23.910
Y-Yeah. I thought we worked very hard,
but we were too optimistic.

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:28.040
I should've... I should've practiced
a lot harder than I did.

00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:31.080
We were talking about nationals
when we're at this level...

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:32.620
I feel very embarra--

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:36.620
It's not embarrassing!
It's not embarrassing at all!

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:41.660
It's true that today's result wasn't
what we wanted,

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:44.790
but we performed the best we could at the time.

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:49.160
There's definitely no need
to be so hard on ourselves!

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:51.250
Takezo...

00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:55.910
It's not working... My words aren't enough.

00:19:55.910 --> 00:19:59.040
I mean every single word, but...

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:02.540
...since I play the koto with them,
my words aren't...

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:05.500
Stop looking so dejected.

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:07.620
Mr. Takinami...

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:11.580
What'd you expect? You guys
messed up during the competition.

00:20:11.580 --> 00:20:13.660
It was a natural outcome.

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:14.870
Like I said before, why do you--?

00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:17.500
--To be honest, I never thought that Mizuhara
would become the trigger

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:19.000
--What?
--To be honest, I never thought that Mizuhara
would become the trigger

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:20.950
for making a comeback.

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:23.910
Nor did I think that Kudo could play
all the way through with that hand,

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:29.160
or that you guys could
recover big together like that.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:33.700
You didn't give your best performance today.

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:37.080
It was better than your best.

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:38.080
What...?

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:43.370
I liked your performance.

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:45.790
It was a good performance.

00:20:45.790 --> 00:20:49.080
You guys can become even better.

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:56.080
My bad. I can only say what I think.

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:07.750
I'm so frustrated!

00:21:07.750 --> 00:21:10.790
We'll win next time for sure!

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:15.160
I'll... I'll practice more
and more to get better!

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:19.080
Next time, I'll perform a lot better than today!

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:22.830
Our next competition is
the national qualifier, right?

00:21:22.830 --> 00:21:24.290
Yeah.

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:26.910
We're definitely gonna go...

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:28.370
...to nationals!

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:37.790
Let's go for sure!

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:41.870
Yep.

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:47.250
All right! We'll make it happen!

00:21:47.250 --> 00:21:49.410
Ahhh, okay, okay. Good luck.

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:51.000
Let's go home already.

00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:55.290
You're not telling us
to quit dreaming today, huh?

00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:58.410
I don't say things that I don't think.

00:23:50.120 --> 00:23:51.910
Next time, "Becoming Aware."

00:23:51.910 --> 00:23:54.500
"#15    Becoming Aware"
